---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy — Paperhint"
  description="What Paperhint collects when you visit this site, why, and how to have it removed."
  canonical="https://paperhint.com/privacy"
>
<Nav />

<article class="prose">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="stamp">Last updated 3 September 2026</p>

  <p>
    This page is about the Paperhint website. It is written to be read, not to
    protect us. If anything here is unclear, write to
    <a href="mailto:support@paperhint.com">support@paperhint.com</a> and we will
    fix the wording.
  </p>

  <div class="box">
    <p>
      <strong>Student data is not on this page.</strong> Nothing a school
      teaches, marks or records goes through this website. A school's own data
      lives in the school's Paperhint account, under an agreement with that
      school, and is never used to train anything.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What we collect here</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>When</th><th>What</th><th>Why</th></tr>
    <tr>
      <td>You fill in the contact form</td>
      <td>Your name, email, school, role, and whatever you wrote</td>
      <td>To reply to you. Nothing else.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>You ask the chat panel something</td>
      <td>Your question, our answer, the page you were on</td>
      <td>To answer, and to learn which questions schools actually have</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Any visit</td>
      <td>Your city and country, and your address shortened to its network</td>
      <td>To know which parts of the country are looking</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Something breaks</td>
      <td>The error, the page, and the browser version</td>
      <td>To fix it. No personal details are attached.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>You accept measurement</td>
      <td>Which pages you opened and what you clicked</td>
      <td>To see which parts of the site are working</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Your address is shortened before it is stored</h2>
  <p>
    We keep the network, not the address: the last part of an IPv4 address is
    dropped, and all but the first half of an IPv6 one. It is enough to tell two
    schools apart. It is not enough to be a street.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies, and the choice you were given</h2>
  <p>
    This site sets no advertising cookies and runs no ad networks. Measurement
    is off until you accept it, and your answer is kept in your own browser's
    storage rather than in a cookie. You can change it at any time:
  </p>
  <p>
    <button type="button" class="btn-ghost" id="resetConsent"
      style="font-family:inherit;font-size:14px;padding:9px 18px;border-radius:999px;
             border:1px solid var(--line);background:transparent;color:var(--ink-soft);cursor:pointer">
      Ask me about cookies again
    </button>
  </p>

  <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Vercel</strong> serves this site and runs its functions.</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong> delivers the emails we send you.</li>
    <li><strong>OpenAI and Google</strong> answer chat questions. Your question is sent to answer it; a school's own data is never sent.</li>
    <li><strong>PostHog</strong> measures site usage, only once you have accepted.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Nobody buys this data from us, because we do not sell it.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiries stay while we are still talking to you and for a year after.
    Chat questions are kept as a rolling window of the most recent few hundred
    and then fall off on their own. Ask us to delete yours sooner and we will.
  </p>

  <h2>Asking us to remove it</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <a href="mailto:support@paperhint.com">support@paperhint.com</a>
    from the address you used, and say what you want removed. You can ask for a
    copy of what we hold, a correction, or deletion. We will do it within 30
    days and tell you when it is done. No form, no ticket number.
  </p>

  <h2>Where we are</h2>
  <p>
    Paperhint is built in Chennai, India. If you are in the EU or UK and think
    we have handled your data badly, you can complain to your local data
    protection authority — but write to us first, because we would rather just
    fix it.
  </p>
</article>

<Footer />
<script is:inline>
  document.getElementById('resetConsent')?.addEventListener('click', function () {
    if (window.PaperhintConsent) window.PaperhintConsent.reset();
  });
</script>
</Base>
